{"id":"659df717-20c5-4930-9065-a0b67dc1a036","companyId":"3d7a91f3-c674-4a9e-862b-11b9698f6686","conversationAgentId":null,"conversationUserId":null,"conversationState":null,"conversationSessionGeneration":0,"conversationBoundaryCommentId":null,"projectId":"dc922baa-82b1-43d3-9f3f-9d7e510f7ee6","projectWorkspaceId":"24d9baf3-c023-4fc7-99f5-6dd2e9ed6d5a","goalId":"9730c5f4-b8c5-47b0-ad0d-cb53e3efa31f","parentId":null,"title":"PR review batch (daily)","titleNeedsGeneration":false,"description":"Purpose: review the day's PR batch and issue verdicts as one batch issue, never one ticket per PR.\nTrigger: cron 0 10 * * * (daily, 10:00) and 30 22 * * * (daily, night shift).\nInputs: open PRs awaiting review; the pr-review-session skill.\nDo:\n1. Follow the pr-review-session skill.\n2. Open ONE issue `PR review batch <date>` covering at most 15 PRs.\n3. Post each verdict as a comment in that batch issue AND on the PR itself: the merge queue's `review-applied` gate reads the PR for a review-pass comment carrying the literal marker `<!-- in-session-review -->`, and the coverage gate reads `reviewed:agent`. A verdict that lives only in the batch issue leaves every PR blocked with 'no review pass left comments'.\n4. Let the launchd merge queue merge approved develop PRs once green and CLEAN - no card needed (updated 12 Oct: every non-promotion PR is owned to merged).\n5. Cancel the per-PR review tickets of every PR in the batch as superseded.\n6. Close the batch issue today.\nOutput: the batch issue with verdict comments, closed the same day, plus the cancelled per-PR review tickets.\nSilent if: no PR is awaiting review - no batch issue is opened and nothing is cancelled.\nOwner / Consumer: EM runs it; only develop->main promotions go to Chris.","status":"done","statusVersion":2,"lastStatusDecisionId":null,"workMode":"standard","harnessKind":null,"priority":"high","reviewPolicy":null,"assigneeAgentId":"6f361355-e086-4a53-a913-b5811e099ab0","assigneeUserId":null,"checkoutRunId":